{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvdvSVFtKd9cbjpUmn3yat","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/153876e10ad3ac8faf9ae5f4672d6f36080abe58fa29ed080d87610f485206e9.json\n-rw------- 1 tom users 8720 Aug 30 12:23 /home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/153876e10ad3ac8faf9ae5f4672d6f36080abe58fa29ed080d87610f485206e9.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task instruments: Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay (rev 4: carrier for proxy first-light fixes 8669bad). Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container/rootfs\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:7d8887178c32e8914bf61d44336b117b52204c5bc0814f6c0c3723f80636028c\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v\"],\"description\":\"All three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.\",\"id\":\"instruments-compile-with-notices\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"Instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill-switches, default off\",\"Notice headers travel with every adapted module\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the FN_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a FN_PROFILE window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env FN_EXPERT_UNION with FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT). Every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. Add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). Boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"instruments\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:152cd533e13f9f9491d2324dd3c370edf7ab76bdfafce33c2195a0fd4ef9488f\",\"title\":\"Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay (rev 4: carrier for proxy first-light fixes 8669bad)\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"c9c4fc23c0e3ceee531e9dc0bf9374c20f2ac7f8\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-b570aaf8311d/instruments\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/instruments-152cd533e13f9f94\",\"taskId\":\"instruments\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/b570aaf8311d/instruments\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \\\"no commit needed\\\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 — CHECKPOINT PURITY (all cp-* tasks). The driver fails a checkpoint whose command mutates tracked files on re-run: \\\"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\\\" (cp-weights burned 3 attempts on this at 07:03-07:10). Discipline: (1) produce your receipt inside your LANE COMMIT (results/receipts/<name>.json, deterministic content); (2) the checkpoint/acceptance command must be IDEMPOTENT and side-effect-free on tracked paths — on re-run over an already-correct base it re-measures and COMPARES; if facts match the committed receipt it must leave every tracked file byte-identical (reuse the receipt's existing ts — NEVER stamp a fresh timestamp onto an unchanged measurement) and exit 0; (3) scratch output goes to untracked temp paths only; (4) if a repo script must change to achieve this, that edit belongs in your lane commit within your ownership paths. Fail receipts still land under results/receipts/failed/ per doctrine.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"id\":3,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/3\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STEER (seq 8, commit-discipline — tally#622 family). Your verification was CORRECT: the instruments deliverables already landed on main via ancestor 4b1d714 and acceptance passes. But the spec-build driver REJECTS a zero-diff squash (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1) — three attempts have already looped this way. A no-new-commit conclusion can never complete this lane. Required: after re-verifying acceptance, land exactly one small NON-EMPTY commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your ownership paths (container/rootfs and tests). Preferred shape: add tests/RECONCILE-instruments-2026-08-30.md — a short note recording the reconcile (HEAD at verification, acceptance command result: py_compile x3, 11 tests, repo suite 50 OK, and that deliverables arrived via ancestor 4b1d714). Do NOT use --allow-empty (the squash still stages no change and fails identically); do NOT touch results/receipts/ or any path outside your ownership; do NOT rewrite the three overlay modules. Then finish normally.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:26.513Z\",\"id\":1,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:26.513Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/1\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[2,3,1],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":11,\"recheckedCursor\":11,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2b5719f-476c-4855-82e3-2b30a75f97fa","uuid":"9b24df4c-08ce-4d86-9c16-c8ea2318736b","timestamp":"2026-08-30T10:23:07.153Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/153876e10ad3ac8faf9ae5f4672d6f36080abe58fa29ed080d87610f485206e9.json\n-rw------- 1 tom users 8720 Aug 30 12:23 /home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/153876e10ad3ac8faf9ae5f4672d6f36080abe58fa29ed080d87610f485206e9.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task instruments: Engagement-proof instruments adapted in