{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYmYmkoyDgA9sENP6pJ1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019hjKNdyKWY1Kn9g9DfQX5j","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/b570aaf8311d/instruments\necho \"=== blob identity vs 4b1d714 ===\"\nfor f in container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py tests/test_instruments.py; do\n  a=$(git rev-parse 4b1d714:$f 2>/dev/null); b=$(git rev-parse HEAD:$f)\n  [ \"$a\" = \"$b\" ] && echo \"identical  $f\" || echo \"DIFFER     $f ($a vs $b)\"\ndone\necho \"=== ancestry ===\"\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor 4b1d714 HEAD && echo \"4b1d714 IS ancestor of HEAD\" || echo \"4b1d714 NOT ancestor\"\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor 237d508 HEAD && echo \"237d508 IS ancestor of HEAD\" || echo \"237d508 NOT ancestor\"\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor 8669bad HEAD && echo \"8669bad IS ancestor of HEAD\" || echo \"8669bad NOT ancestor\"\necho \"=== 8669bad touches ===\"\ngit show --stat --oneline 8669bad | head -20\necho \"=== 8669bad subject/body ===\"\ngit log -1 --format='%s%n%n%b' 8669bad | head -40","description":"Gather lineage and identity facts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2242,"cache_read_input_tokens":37080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2242},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2b5719f-476c-4855-82e3-2b30a75f97fa","uuid":"f821f951-13c3-4113-90aa-63012ce81a61","timestamp":"2026-08-30T10:23:42.044Z","request_id":"req_011CeYmYm1QiBCRfQqnCP7cP"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019hjKNdyKWY1Kn9g9DfQX5j","type":"tool_result","content":"=== blob identity vs 4b1d714 ===\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py\nidentical  tests/test_instruments.py\n=== ancestry ===\n4b1d714 IS ancestor of HEAD\n237d508 IS ancestor of HEAD\n8669bad NOT ancestor\n=== 8669bad touches ===\n8669bad proxy first light: five more fixes proven by local serve to SERVE-READY\n container/Containerfile     | 18 +++++++++\n results/receipts/build.json |  6 +--\n scripts/make-proxy.sh       | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----\n 3 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n=== 8669bad subject/body ===\nproxy first light: five more fixes proven by local serve to SERVE-READY\n\nmake-proxy: (1) engram weight_scale must stream in-place with its module's\nweights (loader groups the stream by module prefix; a trailing-file scale\nis silently dropped) — injected into the sorted inventory as F32 ones,\nonly for the ple-bearing layer (a scale for a module-less layer raises);\n(2) the table's row count is derived by the model (ngram_heads primes >=\nngram_vocab_size_base, padded) — shrink the base to 20000 and reproduce\nthe fork's arithmetic instead of building from token vocab; (3) table\nfiles only for the ple layer — shard tensors named for module-less\nlayers crash the loader.\n\nContainerfile: (4) flash-attn 2.8.3 via the AMD Triton backend\n(FLASH_ATTENTION_TRITON_AMD_ENABLE, --no-deps keeps the pinned\nsubstrate) — the fork's QSA hard-requires flash_attn_varlen_func and no\nROCm wheel exists; (5) amdsmi bridged onto sys.path from\n_rocm_sdk_devel/share/amd_smi via .pth — vllm's get_device_name calls\namdsmi_init unconditionally at fused-MoE kernel-config lookup.\n\nLocal verification: full serve boots to SERVE-READY and answers a\ncompletion (synthetic weights, machinery real: fp8 MoE + QSA triton FA +\nPLE mmap from NVMe + PIECEWISE). build.json re-receipted for the new\nimage; contract fields (torch/triton/fork_commit) unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZLdMFrCnEgtaWKRfxfWWP","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2b5719f-476c-4855-82e3-2b30a75f97fa","uuid":"704e9527-d509-41f5-a364-41fc9a89cc98","timestamp":"2026-08-30T10:23:43.564Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== blob identity vs 4b1d714 ===\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py\nidentical  container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py\nidentical  tests/test_instruments.py\n=== ancestry ===\n4b1d714 IS ancestor of HEAD\n237d508 IS ancestor of HEAD\n8669bad NOT ancestor\n=== 8669bad touches ===\n8669bad proxy first light: five more fixes proven by local serve to SERVE-READY\n container/Containerfile     | 18 +++++++++\n results/receipts/build.json |  6 +--\n scripts/make-proxy.sh       | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----\n 3 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n=== 8669bad subject/body ===\nproxy first light: five more fixes proven by local serve to SERVE-READY\n\nmake-proxy: (1) engram weight_scale must stream in-place with its module's\nweights (loader groups the stream by module prefix; a trailing-file scale\nis silently dropped) — injected into the sorted inventory as F32 ones,\nonly for the ple-bearing layer (a scale for a module-less layer raises);\n(2) the table's row count is derived by the model (ngram_heads primes >=\nngram_vocab_size_base, padded) — shrink the base to 20000 and reproduce\nthe fork's arithmetic instead of building from token vocab; (3) table\nfiles only for the ple layer — shard tensors named for module-less\nlayers crash the loader.\n\nContainerfile: (4) flash-attn 2.8.3 via the AMD Triton backend\n(FLASH_ATTENTION_TRITON_AMD_ENABLE, --no-deps keeps the pinned\nsubstrate) — the fork's QSA hard-requires flash_attn_varlen_func and no\nROCm wheel exists; (5) amdsmi bridged onto sys.path from\n_rocm_sdk_devel/share/amd_smi via .pth — vllm's get_device_name calls\namdsmi_init unconditionally at fused-MoE kernel-config lookup.\n\nLocal verification: full serve boots to SERVE-READY and answers a\ncompletion (synthetic weights, machinery real: fp8 MoE + QSA triton FA +\nPLE mmap from NVMe + PIECEWISE). build.json re-receipted for the new\nimage; contract fields (torch/triton/fork_commit) unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZLdMFrCnEgtaWKRfxfWWP","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
